## Rows skipped (with reason)
ta-a 6  (003 restore "அதிகபட்ச" / maximum compensation). SKIP. RULEBOOK-FIX R3 explicitly rewrote this exact
        sentence to "the compensation the facts and evidence support", and ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids making a
        result sentence positive again. The reviewer is asking to revert a supervisor rule.
ta-a 34 ("TWD 1.57M" → TWD 15,70,000). SKIP per ACCEPTED-ROUND and R12: the figure is pinned byte-identical by
        a test, and lakh grouping is not parsed by the checker (R14).
ta-b 36 (strip the U+200B zero-width spaces in 013 and 015). SKIP — the checker asserts ZWSP parity against the
        Korean source (checkBlocks: `ZWSP ${sourceZwsp} → ${targetZwsp}` is a FAIL, not a warning) and the
        Korean originals carry exactly 5 in 013 and 3 in 015 (003:52, 005:8, 006:4, 008:10, 009:5 likewise).
        Removing them turns 18/18 PASS into 2 FAILs. Verified by reading scripts/check-column-translation.mjs
        lines 2615–2642 and counting ZWSP in src/content/columns/013,015.
ta-b 37 (make the four-language list uniform: "…ஜப்பானியம், கொரியம் ஆகிய மொழிகளில்"). SKIP — ACCEPTED-ROUND:
        "Requests to translate the four consultation language names differently from the locale's own
        established form → keep one consistent form across the pack and columns." The pack's established form
        is "கொரிய மொழி" (and the picker label "கொரிய மொழி (한국어)"); changing only the columns would break that
        consistency, and changing the pack too would touch the pinned consultation-notice strings.
ta-a 3  — applied only in part, see the disagreements section.

## Rows I believe the reviewer got wrong (not applied as written)
1. ta-a 3 — "restore 'generally' (தற்போது நீதிமன்றங்கள் பொதுவாகச் சுமார் 3 மாதச் சிறை விதிக்கின்றன)". The
   contradiction the reviewer names is real, but the fix he proposes re-states current sentencing practice as a
   general rule, which is what R3 was written to remove ("in some judgments about 3 months has been imposed;
   there is no typical or guaranteed outcome"). I removed the contradiction from the other half instead: the
   disclaimer no longer says "not a usual result" (which clashed with "in some judgments") but "does not
   predict the outcome of your case". Meaning kept, R3 kept, digits kept.
2. ta-a 6 — "restore அதிகபட்ச / maximum compensation". Same conflict with R3; not applied (see skips).
3. ta-a 1 — the suggested "அந்த அதிர்ஷ்டம் கிடைக்கவில்லை" (that luck) sits badly next to the preceding sentence,
   which R3 had already rewritten from "obtained a high severance" to "was able to establish the entitlement
   under the law": law-based entitlement immediately followed by "luck" reads as undercutting it, and R8 rules
   out 'luck' as a rendering of a favourable outcome elsewhere. I used "அந்த வாய்ப்பு கிடைக்கவில்லை" (did not get
   that opportunity), which carries "were not as fortunate" without the luck frame.
4. ta-b 5 — the reviewer scopes "உறுதியான = specific" to 010–018 (28×). ta-a reviewed 001–009 and did not flag a
   single one there, and several of those are genuinely "fixed/definite" (001 "உறுதியான வரிசை அல்லது கால அளவு
   அல்ல", 002 "உறுதியான காலத்தை வைத்து", 003 "பாதுகாப்பு உறுதியான பிறகு"). I therefore swept 010–018 only and
   left 001–009 for a later round rather than guess at 22 unflagged instances.
5. ta-b 22 — the suggested rewrite reads "உண்மையான முடிவு" as a list item. The English is "The actual outcome
   requires a review of …", i.e. it is the subject. I kept the reviewer's surface wording (comma after
   "உண்மையான முடிவு", closing "ஆகியவற்றை … தீர்மானிக்கப்படும்") but the four-item object list is what is reviewed.
6. ta-b 20/33 — listed as two rows but it is a single occurrence in 016; fixed once.

